{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-2670"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of optical instruments and photographic equipment"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "2670"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :optical-instrument/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:consumer-safety :worker-safety :materials-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :optical-instrument-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :eda :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "OpticalInstrAdvisor ⊣ Optical Instrument Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor for optical instrument and photographic equipment
 manufacturing (lens-grinding/optics-assembly/testing lines producing
 lenses, binoculars, microscopes, telescopes, cameras and projectors)
 -- not direct lens-grinding/assembly-line-equipment control authority
 and not laser-safety-classification-body regulatory authority. Four
 ops (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Thirteen concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct lens-grinding/
 assembly-line-equipment control), permanent equipment-actuate block,
 permanent laser-safety-classification-authority block (this actor
 never self-issues an IEC 60825-1 laser safety class certification),
 independent equipment verification/registration before maintenance
 scheduling, independent batch verification/registration before
 shipment coordination, independent shipment-quantity recompute
 against the batch's own logged production quantity, double-schedule
 guard, instrument-class validation, resolution-test plausibility
 validation, and defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern
 flagging (materials-safety/precision-defect/laser-alignment-hazard)
 ALWAYS escalates to a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch`
 is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
 governor-clean."}
